# Codebase store: checked spec

The checkable half of [CODEBASE-STORE.md](../../docs/spec/CODEBASE-STORE.md), which explains each point, written
in the order of the process (D92): requirements, then the APIs and laws they rest on, then the
tests and theorems. Every requirement names its evidence. `deus add` compiles the
[Laws](#laws) section next to [`deus/codebase.deus`](../../deus/codebase.deus), and
`deus mdl Codebase.Spec` checks that the APIs exist with these types, that every
law and test it names passes, and that each law states what the spec says.

## Extensions

| Term | URI |
| --- | --- |
| `api` | `org.dxos.deus.api@1.0` |
| `law` | `org.dxos.deus.law@1.0` |
| `req` | `org.dxos.deus.req@1.0` |

## APIs

```mdl
api A-1: the object store
  signatures:
  - Codebase.put : Text -> Sexp -> {IO} Text
  - Codebase.readObject : Text -> Text -> {IO} Option Sexp
  - Codebase.objectPath : Text -> Text -> Text
  - Codebase.dependencies : Sexp -> List Text
  - Codebase.layerOf : Sexp -> Text
  - Codebase.mayDependOn : Text -> List Text
```

```mdl
api A-5: metadata shared by names with one hash
  signatures:
  - Codebase.metaFor : Text -> Sexp -> Sexp
  - Codebase.mergeMeta : Option Sexp -> Sexp -> Sexp
```

```mdl
api A-2: namespace snapshots
  signatures:
  - Codebase.putNamespace : Text -> Map Text Entry -> {IO} Text
  - Codebase.readNamespace : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Map Text Entry
  - Codebase.lookupName : Text -> Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Option Entry
```

```mdl
api A-3: history and branches
  signatures:
  - Codebase.init : Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Unit
  - Codebase.commit : Text -> Map Text Entry -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Codebase.causalToSexp : Causal -> Sexp
  - Codebase.causalFromSexp : Sexp -> Causal
  - Codebase.merge : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} MergeResult
```

```mdl
api A-4: Codebase definitions other namespaces use
  signatures:
  - Codebase.allObjects : Text -> {IO} List Text
  - Codebase.ancestors : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Map Text Unit
  - Codebase.branchHead : Text -> Text -> {IO} Option Text
  - Codebase.branches : Text -> {IO} List Text
  - Codebase.commitComments : Text -> Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Codebase.commitPrior : Text -> Sexp -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Codebase.commitTasks : Text -> Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Codebase.current : Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Map Text Entry
  - Codebase.currentBranch : Text -> {IO} Text
  - Codebase.diffNamespaces : Text -> Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} List (Text, (Option Entry, Option Entry))
  - Codebase.headOf : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Codebase.history : Text -> Text -> Int -> {IO, Throw Text} List (Text, Causal)
  - Codebase.isCodebase : Text -> {IO} Bool
  - Codebase.layers : List (Text, (Text, Bool))
  - Codebase.metaField : Option Sexp -> Text -> Option Sexp
  - Codebase.metaList : Option Sexp -> Text -> List Sexp
  - Codebase.migrate : Text -> {IO, Throw Text} (Int, Int)
  - Codebase.nameIndex : Map Text Entry -> Map Text Text
  - Codebase.namesByHash : Map Text Entry -> Map Text (List Text)
  - Codebase.namesOf : Map Text Entry -> Text -> List Text
  - Codebase.parentsOf : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} List Text
  - Codebase.readCausal : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Causal
  - Codebase.readMeta : Text -> Text -> {IO} Option Sexp
  - Codebase.recordEntries : Text -> Text -> {IO} List (Text, (Text, Text))
  - Codebase.rewrite : Sexp -> Map Text Text -> Sexp
  - Codebase.setBranch : Text -> Text -> Text -> {IO} Unit
  - Codebase.snapshotsOf : Causal -> List Text
  - Codebase.store : Text -> Batch -> {IO} Unit
  - Codebase.validBranch : Text -> Bool
  - Codebase.writeMeta : Text -> Text -> Sexp -> {IO} Unit
  - Codebase.writeObject : Text -> Text -> Sexp -> {IO} Unit
```

## Hashes and object files

```mdl
law L-1: an object is stored under the SHA-256 of its canonical text
  theorem: Codebase.Spec.putNamesByHash
  evidence: test
```

```mdl
req R-1: a file under objects/ is the canonical text and a new line, at objects/<first two>/<hash>
  by: Codebase.Spec.putNamesByHash
```

```mdl
req R-2: builtin hashes (starting with #) are never dependencies
  by: Codebase.Spec.builtinsAreNotDependencies
```

## Namespace snapshots

```mdl
law L-2: a namespace reads back as written, as a whole and name by name
  theorem: Codebase.Spec.namespaceRoundTrip
  statement: (names : List Text) : Codebase.Spec.readsBack (Codebase.Spec.namespaceOf names) = true
```

```mdl
law L-3: a snapshot's hash depends only on its names and entries
  theorem: Codebase.Spec.snapshotIgnoresOrder
```

```mdl
req R-3: nodes past 64 items split into parts, and still read back
  by: Codebase.Spec.wideNamespaceRoundTrip
```

```mdl
req R-4: the empty namespace hashes to f126eadc…
  by: Codebase.Spec.emptyNamespaceHash
```

## History nodes and branches

```mdl
law L-4: a history node reads back as written
  theorem: Codebase.Spec.causalRoundTrip
```

```mdl
req R-5: deus init always writes the same first node
  by: Codebase.Spec.initIsAlwaysTheSame
```

```mdl
req R-6: a commit whose snapshot equals its parent's leaves the branch where it was
  by: Codebase.Spec.unchangedCommitWritesNothing
```

## Merge

```mdl
req R-7: a name changed on one side takes that side, a removal included
  by: Codebase.Spec.mergeTakesEachSidesChange | Codebase.Spec.mergeTakesTheirRemoval
```

```mdl
req R-8: a name changed differently on both sides is a conflict, and nothing is written
  by: Codebase.Spec.mergeReportsConflicts
```

```mdl
req R-9: when ours is an ancestor of theirs, the merge fast-forwards
  by: Codebase.Spec.mergeFastForwards
```

## Updates

```mdl
req R-13: an update rehashes every definition that depends on a changed one, including one in the update whose text did not change
  by: Codebase.Spec.dependentsFollowAnUpdate | Codebase.Spec.unchangedTextFollowsRehashedDependent
```

```mdl
req R-15: an update that changes only a definition's metadata (its doc comment or attributes) names the definition, and one that changes nothing, changes the hash, or renames only locals does not name it as metadata
  by: Codebase.Spec.docChangeListed | Codebase.Spec.attributeChangeListed | Codebase.Spec.sameMetadataUnlisted | Codebase.Spec.changedHashUnlisted | Codebase.Spec.localRenameUnlisted
```

Core has no names, so two definitions with one body share a hash and one metadata file (task 62f3f4d0). The file
names its owner, the name that last wrote it; every other name keeps its own fields (doc, comments, locals,
attributes, annotation) in a `(for "<name>" …)` entry, and readers take a name's view of the file with
`Codebase.metaFor`. Only the inferred scheme is shared.

```mdl
req R-16: names that share a hash keep their own doc comments, whether added together or apart, and a name's update replaces only its own; a name whose fields match the owner's changes nothing
  by: Codebase.Spec.sharedHashKeepsEachDoc | Codebase.Spec.laterAddKeepsOtherDoc | Codebase.Spec.ownUpdateReplacesOwnDoc | Codebase.Spec.unsharedHasNoEntries | Codebase.Spec.sameFieldsKeepTheOwner
```

```mdl
req R-17: when a definition in an update takes over another's old body, and so its old hash, what the update compiled keeps calling it, while dependents outside the update follow the name they called
  by: Codebase.Spec.extractedBodyKeepsItsName | Codebase.Spec.dependentFollowsTheName
```

```mdl
req R-18: an update that drops a structure's field, a type's constructor or an ability's operation removes that name too, and keeps every name the update still declares
  by: Codebase.Spec.droppedFieldLeavesNoAccessor | Codebase.Spec.droppedConstructorIsRemoved | Codebase.Spec.droppedOperationIsRemoved | Codebase.Spec.keptMembersStay
```

```mdl
req R-19: an update whose change leaves a dependent outside it ill-typed fails, names that dependent and the definition it calls, and commits nothing; a change its dependents still type-check against goes through
  by: Codebase.Spec.illTypedDependentFails | Codebase.Spec.welltypedDependentFollows
```

A recursive group is hashed as one cycle, so changing one member gives every member a new hash. When the
change brings a new member into the group, the batch's hashes are not final: the old members it calls
are rehashed, and the batch's members are rehashed again after them. A dependent outside the group must
follow the final hashes, not the batch's (task f308d451).

```mdl
req R-20: after an update adds a member to a recursive group, every dependent outside the group references only current hashes
  by: Codebase.Spec.groupGainsAMember
```

```mdl
req R-21: two `Js.import` bindings with one body but different declared types are refused, naming both, since they share one object and the js target would give both one codec; two at the same type are aliases and are kept
  by: Codebase.Spec.sharedBindingRefused | Codebase.Spec.sameTypedBindingsKept | Codebase.Spec.sharedBindingInOneBatchRefused
```

```mdl
req R-22: `deus update` skips a source file whose text the last update compiled, while nothing else has changed the codebase since; the result is what a full update (`--fresh`) stores
  by: Codebase.Spec.skippingMatchesFullUpdate | Codebase.Spec.unchangedFileReappliedAfterOtherUpdate
```

```mdl
req R-10: tasks merge field by field; labels and links merge as sets
  by: Codebase.Spec.tasksMergeFieldByField | Codebase.Spec.tasksMergeLabelsAsSets | Codebase.Spec.tasksMergeConflict
```

```mdl
req R-14: comment threads merge as unions: a thread one side changed takes that side, and comments both sides added are all kept, ours first
  by: Codebase.Spec.commentThreadsMergeAsUnions | Codebase.Spec.commentThreadsTakeTheChangedSide
```

## Layers

```mdl
req R-11: each layer depends only on the layers the table allows
  by: Codebase.Spec.layersFollowTheTable
```

```mdl
req R-12: add and update refuse a batch that crosses layers
  by: Codebase.Spec.codeCannotNameATest | Codebase.Spec.codeMayNotDependOnTests | Codebase.Spec.testsMayDependOnCode
```

## Laws

Laws about pure functions are theorems; laws about the store run it in the deterministic
simulation, so they read and write no real files.

The laws are the definitions under `Codebase.Spec`: `deus ls Codebase.Spec.` lists them and `deus view` prints them.
